{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles felt like a natural next choice because familiar, melodic rock connects with my classic rock collections and my interest in greatest hits.",
    "Carpenters and Lesley Gore connected with different parts of my listening: the gentle melodies of Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie, and the mid-sixties songs in AM Gold."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Pat Benatar, Journey and Styx fit my broader taste, but I wanted softer songs this visit, so their classic rock connection alone did not make them immediate choices.",
    "I could not judge Greatest Hits, Vol. 1 and 2 without knowing the artist; the compilation title alone gave me no reason to expect music I would enjoy."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices leaned too heavily on my interest in classic rock without enough distinction between gentler melodies and more forceful rock.",
    "My repeated interest in greatest hits seemed to count too much on its own; whose songs are included matters more than the compilation format."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie listening points toward gentle, melodic songs, which made Carpenters especially appealing today.",
    "Liking several related artists does not mean I want all their collections at once; choosing Carpenters made Bread less urgent even though both fit my taste."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in familiar melodic hits, but gave too little weight to my softer mood and selective choices today."
}"}
